recommended_synthesis:
Ship A's architecture, add B's search rigour and a thin slice of C's sync. It is one installable SvelteKit static PWA (TS 6, JS <= 90 KB brotli) for phone and desktop. Its hot paths, search and write, never touch the network and work fully offline after the first visit. The catalog stays A's static, content-hashed snapshot on Cloudflare static assets: a manifest checked at most every 12 h, the core, 14 daily deltas and 1,024 details shards with library_capsule/header paths and dates. GitHub Actions builds it from the keyed IStoreService/GetAppList (daily if_modified_since delta, weekly full reconcile) plus the keyless GetItems (ES context, <= 200 ids per call, about 0.4 req/s, global pause on 429). Move the minimal enrichment into M1: type 0 only, coming-soon/early-access, content descriptors 3/4, review_count → pop, Spanish name. That way ranking and the +18 filter exist from day one. Refuse to publish unless C-style smoke queries pass on the built index. The catalog is games-only by default. Optionally add the few thousand most-reviewed DLC/expansions (Shadow of the Erdtree, Phantom Liberty) under a 'DLC' badge, ranked below base games; never demos or soundtracks. Explorar keeps A's virtual list of all ~196.6k games.

Search runs in a module Web Worker over A's bitset word-prefix index (ids in static-rank order, precomputed one-letter bitsets, early exit). The fold is corrected: strip ™ ℠ ® © and every apostrophe form before NFKD, using B's order but A/C's deletion (never B's apostrophe→space). Then strip accents, lowercase, apply a ligature map and turn punctuation into spaces. Index both base and Spanish names, roman numerals 1-20 and CJK/Kana bigrams (C). Add an article-stripped title key and acronyms: B's curated CSV plus generated initials of 3+ characters for the ~5k most-reviewed games, so cs2, rdr2 and gta5 hit. Candidates are the prefix walk (<= 200), plus the exact-title map, plus a title-start range on the article-stripped key. They are ranked in tiers (exact or exact acronym > title-start > all tokens as word-prefixes in order > substring), with popularity used only inside a tier. Coming-soon is never penalized, delisted games go last with 'Retirado', and +18 is off by default. Compact-substring matching and uFuzzy run only when hits are scarce, and 'En tu agenda' matches come first. For readiness, split the core into a popularity head (~top 20k, ≈ 0.2-0.3 MB brotli) fetched first and the tail fetched after load; this replaces C's server search tier with a static file. Persist the built typed arrays per catalog seq (C), so a cached restart restores in about 0.1-0.4 s instead of rebuilding for 1-1.5 s on phones. Manual title-only add and link paste work before any catalog, and such titles auto-link when they match exactly one game (B).

Capture: the agenda opens with a bottom 'Apuntar' bar within thumb reach (C). In the overlay, tapping the whole row (>= 56 px) adds to Quiero jugar in one tap (Enter on desktop). Long-press or Alt+Enter opens the Jugando/Completado/Platinado/Comprado/Próximo picker, and the field keeps focus for bursts. Saved games show their state chip instead of '+'. Every action gets an undo toast, never a dialog.
- Android: the installed PWA's share target auto-adds with undo, plus the 'Apuntar juego' shortcut (A).
- iOS: the 'Pegar enlace' chip, plus B's share-sheet Shortcut that POSTs the URL to a write-only, revocable /inbox token.
- Desktop: '/', Ctrl+K, Shift+Enter and Ctrl+V-anywhere link parsing (C). Pin the installed PWA to the taskbar so Win+1 brings it up with the input focused. Add a bookmarklet that opens /share?url= in the same Chromium profile.
- Only if measured desktop capture misses 3 s: add B's Quick-add as a thin Tauri 2 shell over the same build. It has a global Ctrl+Shift+Space (never Ctrl+Alt, because of AltGr), a pre-created hidden window and clipboard-link preselect. It is one more sync client, never a second engine.

Data lives in Dexie entries with A's model: 5 exclusive Estados and an open flag set. Platinado sets Completado and completedAt once but survives a later replay; Comprado; Próximo pinned. Entries also have a note, auto-stamped editable dates and tombstones. Add B's user-defined labels and keyboard shortcuts (1-5, P/C/N, Ctrl+Z with multi-step undo). A tap updates memory and paints in under 16 ms, then persists. Entries carry their own title and cover, so the agenda paints before the catalog loads. Because capture happens on both devices, pull a lean sync into the prototype instead of leaving it for M6:
- B's pseudonymous pairing (a 256-bit secret shared by QR or URL fragment; the server stores only its hash) on one D1 (EU) ops table;
- push/pull of A's per-field HLC change log;
- single-tab sync via Web Locks on focus, online and visibility (C);
- the /inbox.
Steam OpenID (with C's PKCE ticket) and imports come later. Sequence: M1 search and capture on both devices, with popularity; M2 states, flags and covers; M3 capture surfaces, head/tail core, persisted index, sync and inbox; then edge details/resolve, Steam import and the optional Tauri Quick-add.

CI gates:
- keystroke→paint p95 <= 50 ms at CDP 4x over ~600 keystrokes (A), with C's long-task observer failing any main-thread task over 50 ms while typing or adding;
- tap→feedback <= 100 ms (Event Timing);
- INP p75 <= 200 ms;
- LCP <= 2.5 s (Lighthouse gate at 2.0 s; the catalog is fetched in the worker after load);
- first-visit search <= 1.5 s after load;
- cached restart: agenda <= 1 s, search <= 1 s.
Measure on a real mid-range Android at each milestone exit, and use A's in-app p50/p95 panel for the iPhone. Golden sets are A's 100 Spanish queries plus B's 2,000 random exact names (>= 99% top-5) and the 4-letter prefixes of the 1,000 most popular games (>= 90% top-10). They explicitly include queries without apostrophes, acronyms, roman numerals, Spanish names and coming-soon games.
